{{<shell}}{{$content}}
<h1>Settings</h1>
<p class="hint"><strong>This is a report, not an editor.</strong> Every setting here was read once,
  from a file, before this server opened its socket &mdash; and never again. That is deliberate: a
  half-applied policy is worse than no server, and nothing on a request path should be able to
  change what a domain is. What it costs is being able to see it, which is what this screen is for.</p>
<p class="hint">To change anything: edit the file named above each block and restart. A key this
  server does not recognise stops it from starting, which is the intended failure mode &mdash; a
  typo is a setting somebody believes is applied and is not.</p>
<p class="hint mono">community file: {{configFile}} &middot; server file:
  &lt;root&gt;/{{serverFile}} &middot; schema {{schemaVersion}} &middot; {{version}}</p>

{{#groups}}
<h2>{{title}}</h2>
<p class="hint">{{about}} <span class="dim">&mdash; {{file}}</span></p>
<div class="scroller"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>key</th><th>now</th><th>what it does</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>{{#rows}}<tr>
    <td class="mono">{{key}}</td>
    <td>{{#bool}}{{#on}}<span class="pill blue">on</span>{{/on}}{{#off}}<span class="pill dim">off</span>{{/off}}{{/bool}}{{^bool}}{{#unset}}<span class="dim">not set</span>{{/unset}}{{^unset}}<span class="mono">{{value}}</span>{{/unset}}{{/bool}}</td>
    <td class="dim">{{hint}}</td>
  </tr>{{/rows}}</tbody>
</table></div>
{{/groups}}
{{/content}}{{/shell}}
